From 7c03c1b23fb3289cdb6a1758830b69623d41caac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:04:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information polished, rows and plate as
 high as they need
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design B, polished after the first screenshots:

 - A row whose value may take more than one line (HadesPanelRowWide,
   HadesPanelRowText) is as high as what it shows: a grouplist of automatic
   height (CGUIControlGroupList::GetHeight()) with a text box of automatic
   height for the value (CGUITextBox::UpdateInfo()). A value of one line no
   longer leaves an empty line under it ("Colour", "Metadata sent", "Sent
   as") and a long one is not cut. Its name takes one line beside it; four
   names are said shorter for that (41889 to 41892), and two rows that scrolled
   a long value wrap it now (the passes, the blocks sent): no row of the panel
   moves its text.
 - The plate is exactly as high as the page shown needs, in every state and
   language: under each column, a ghost of it (the same rows with the same
   conditions and heights, the text box of a row of automatic height in no
   colour) paints the plate behind the rows and under the last one, the whole
   width of the panel; the ghosts are drawn before the columns, so the plate
   ends under the longest. Fixed heights left bands of up to 114 px wherever a
   page showed fewer rows than it can. The foot of the overview (the machine
   and the output of this video) and of the Dolby Vision page (the last 10 s
   and the output) goes above the columns, under the strip and under the
   table, where its place does not depend on the rows; the output stays a
   press of Down from the tabs.
 - No middle dots in what the panel shows: commas, words or brackets instead
   ("3840x2160p, 23.976 fps", "H.265, 58.2 Mb/s", "4.1 ms (37.6 ms spare)",
   "HDMI-A-1 (nvidia-drm)", "9% (5800 / 63200 MB)", "100% (data 41%)",
   "IEC 61937, 8 × 192 kHz", "18%, 46 °C"); #31828 is "RGB 8-bit, DV 12-bit
   4:2:2". The last 10 s of Dolby Vision are three fields, as the machine on
   the overview.
 - Overview: the mark beside "Hades" on the strip, which read as a sign of
   loading, and the warm stub at the top left of the plate are gone (the cold
   line of the rim stays); "TV offers" takes one line.
 - Video: under "HDR metadata sent", native Dolby Vision says why there is none
   (41886), and a Dolby Vision video sent as SDR says that none is sent; Kodi's
   screen resolution only where there is no mode (the mode above says it
   exactly); the depth of a Dolby Vision output shorter (41887).
 - Dolby Vision: the composer as two rows (41884, 41885); the passes of the
   graphics card go to the system page, beside its time and headroom; the
   Spanish of "mastered brighter than the TV" shorter, to take two lines.
 - Audio: Kodi's audio channels and audio stream are left out of the sound out:
   they said again what the sound of the film says (the same
   Player.Process(audiochannels); the same rate and bits of the data cache as
   hades.audio.src*). kHz and kb/s everywhere.
 - System: three columns of about as many rows: the frames of the last 10 s,
   the dropped and the skipped go to a column "Playback" (41888) with the cache
   and the queues; the screen resolution is the mode of the output where there
   is one (it was cut in two lines).

system/hades made again (make-playerinfo.py --check clean).
